# ============================================================================
# This repository is intended to become a PUBLIC CyberAgents Exchange listing.
# The Exchange auto-scans the FULL git history for secrets, and rejection is
# automatic. Nothing here may be relaxed without a deliberate decision logged
# in NOTES.md.
# ============================================================================

# --- credentials / secrets ---
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*service_account*.json
*service-account*.json
credentials*.json
client_secret*.json
.env
.env.*
secrets*
*.token
*.apikey

# --- real mail and real alert data: NEVER commit ---
# Real reported-phishing content contains employee addresses (FERPA-adjacent)
# and live campaign indicators belonging to the employer.
# Real mail must never be committed - that is the data policy, and the Exchange
# scans full history. The exceptions below are generated corpora using RFC 2606
# reserved domains, produced by a committed generator, so they are reproducible
# and contain nobody's mail. Adding another corpus means adding another negation
# here, and tests/test_doc_references.py fails the build if a corpus the tests
# consume is not actually tracked.
*.eml
!fixtures/synthetic/*.eml
!fixtures/adversarial/*.eml
!fixtures/attachments/*.eml
*.mbox
*.msg
output*.txt
alerts*.csv
comparison_*.csv
*_comparison*.csv
ground_truth*.csv
labels*.csv

# --- run roots, receipts, journals and ledgers: operator state, never committed ---
# A run root is caller-chosen (`--root`), so `tenable-email run --root .` inside
# this repository would otherwise write receipts/ and journal.jsonl into the
# working tree. Against the live feed those carry real message-IDs and sender
# addresses, and the Exchange scans full git history for exactly that.
receipts/
journal.jsonl
run-root/
ledger/
ledger.sqlite3
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal

# --- downloaded public evaluation corpora: fetched, never committed ---
# Licenses include CC-BY-NC-SA, CC-BY-SA, OpenRAIL, GPL and LGPL, and one set
# declares no license at all. See docs/EVAL-SUITES.md.
eval/internal/

# --- local working data and scratch ---
.scratch/
data/
private/
cache/
*.local.*
*.bak
*.bak-*

# --- python ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- model artifacts (download, do not version) ---
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
models/

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Review bundles and build output - regenerated, never committed
dist/
